<title>USA: LTV union to hold own shareholder meeting.</title>
<headline>LTV union to hold own shareholder meeting.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Steelworkers of America said on Thursday that union members who work for LTV Corp and also own company stock will hold their own shareholders' meeting on April 7, presided over by U.S. Rep. Dennis Kucinich.</p>
<p>The union said the meeting in Cleveland is a response to the company holding its annual meeting in Delaware.</p>
<p>Joining Kucinich, who represents Cleveland in Congress, will be U.S. Rep. David Oberstar and U.S. Sen. Paul Wellstone, both of Minnesota.</p>
<p>The union said the LTV board was also invited.</p>
<p>LTV officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
